  "id": "https://openrel.eu/vocab/sources",
  "title": "OpenREL Normalized Source Registry",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Deduplicated and granularly referenced legal, regulatory, and technical sources. The draft repeated generic domain URLs (e.g., https://eosc-portal.eu/) across 90+ sections without specificity. This registry replaces those with unique identifiers, precise article/clause references where applicable, and validated links.",
  "deduplication_notes": [
    "The draft referenced 'https://eosc-portal.eu/' as a source for 46+ distinct sections without any article or document specificity. This has been decomposed into distinct EOSC policy documents.",
    "GDPR was cited inconsistently as 'GDPR Overview', 'GDPR Ethical Guidelines', 'GDPR Ethical Data Handling Principles', etc. — all pointing to gdpr-info.eu. Merged into one entry with article-level granularity.",
    "Creative Commons was cited multiple times as both a licensing framework and an 'ethical reuse' source. Merged into one entry.",
    "OECD was cited generically across 30+ sections. Decomposed into distinct OECD publications where identifiable."
  ],
